<Base title="About | Waking Matter" description="Founded by Aditya Vikram Singh. Building systems for agents that improve with experience." canonical="https://wakingmatter.com/about/" current="about">
  <main id="content" class="wrap">
    <header class="page-hero"><p class="label">About</p><h1>Experience should become capability.</h1><p class="lede">Waking Matter is building systems for agents that improve with experience. Useful learning should carry forward, change the next decision and remain open to correction.</p></header>
    <div class="prose-page split"><p class="label">Our conviction</p><div class="measure">
      <p>Intelligence should accumulate. The effort spent solving a problem should make the next encounter more capable, not just leave a longer transcript.</p>
      <p>We work on the systems that connect experience to action: memory and state, provenance, evaluation and adaptive control. That includes deciding when prior learning deserves to be trusted, and when to revise it or begin again.</p>
      <p>Our public work includes <a href="https://github.com/avs-io/agent-memory-contracts">Agent Memory Contracts</a>, a Python library that makes the boundary between extracted claims and trusted memory explicit. The <a href="/research/">research questions</a> set out the next challenge: showing when retained experience improves decisions in repeated work.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="prose-page split"><p class="label">Founder</p><div class="measure">
      <p>Waking Matter was founded by <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/-aditya-vikram-singh/">Aditya Vikram Singh</a>.</p>
      <p>His earlier work spans strategy at Accenture, venture investing at Rukam Capital and corporate development at Noise. Across those roles, the recurring questions were how to make decisions with incomplete information, allocate scarce resources and update when reality disagrees. At Waking Matter, those questions become systems to build and test.</p>
      <p>Waking Matter is at the start of a long program, and we are looking for collaborators with hard recurring workflows. If agents keep rediscovering context, repeating mistakes or failing when facts change in your work, write to <a href="mailto:hello@wakingmatter.com">hello@wakingmatter.com</a>.</p>
    </div></div>
  </main>
</Base>
